# Attributes that two project rules would otherwise disagree about.

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Archived licence texts are VERBATIM and must never be tidied.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# ADR-0012 and `licenses/README.md`: "Licence texts are copied verbatim, never summarised", so that
# a later reader can compare our copy against upstream's and get a byte-for-byte answer.
#
# The pre-commit hook runs `git diff --cached --check`, which rejects trailing whitespace. The SIL
# Open Font License 1.1, as published by SIL and as shipped in every Noto release, has a trailing
# space on the line "fonts, including any derivative works, can be bundled, embedded,". Stripping it
# would make `licenses/ofl-1.1/LICENCE.txt` differ from the licence it claims to reproduce -- which
# is precisely the thing the archive exists to prevent -- and would break the hash comparison in
# `docs/font-provenance.md`.
#
# So the whitespace check is turned off for archived licence texts and for nothing else. It still
# applies to `licenses/THIRD-PARTY-ASSETS.md`, which this project generates.
licenses/*/LICENCE.txt -whitespace

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Asset binaries
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Declared rather than left to Git's heuristic. A font or a compiled effect that was ever treated as
# text -- by an eol conversion on a Windows clone, say -- would fail its manifest hash with no
# obvious cause, and `assets-src/` is going to fill up with binaries.
*.ttf  binary
*.otf  binary
*.ttc  binary
*.glb  binary
*.png  binary
*.wav  binary
*.xnb  binary
*.cnb  binary
